# Review routing. Anything not matched below still falls to the
# catch-all, so this file is about making the *reason* for a review
# explicit, not about adding gates.
#
# Syntax: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

*                               @mastersingh24

# Frozen contracts. Changing one of these is a negotiation with
# downstream consumers, not a code change — the guardian tests exist to
# force the conversation, and the review is where it happens.
/docs/DESIGN.md                 @mastersingh24
/docs/signal-schema-v1.md       @mastersingh24
/docs/cli-stability-policy.md   @mastersingh24
/pkg/engine/fingerprint.go      @mastersingh24
/pkg/inject/schema/             @mastersingh24

# Security boundaries. The sanitizer is the one place a Secret value
# could reach an output surface; the RBAC manifests define everything
# the sentinel is allowed to see.
/pkg/emit/sanitize.go           @mastersingh24
/pkg/exempt/                    @mastersingh24
/deploy/                        @mastersingh24
/SECURITY.md                    @mastersingh24

